                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Det(A) = \big(Pf(A)\big)^2
              follows readily (cf.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/2705327/58526"} Math.SE:a/2705327
            %p
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#PfaffianStateOfFractionalQuantumHallEffect Pfaffian state of fractional quantum Hall systems
          %p
            Pfaffians appear in the expression of certain multiparticle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+functions"} wave functions
            generalizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laughlin+wavefunctions"} Laughlin wavefunctions
            modeling
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+states"} ground states
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+systems"} fractional quantum Hall systems
          %p
            Prominent here is the
            %em pfaffian state
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "Laughlin+wavefunction#MooreRead91"}> Moore &amp; Read 1991 (5.1)
            \&amp;rbrack; of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
          %blockquote
            %p
              (In practice,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is a humongous “macroscopic” number on the scale of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Avogadro+constant"} Avogadro constant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even
              without any conceivable restriction of practical generality.)
          %p
            of spinless (or rather: spin-polarized)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            = succeed "\u201D-)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunction"} wave
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"}
              configuration space of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              points
            in the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"}> complex
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
          #eq:MooreReadPfaffianState.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
