          %p
            This observation is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Laughlin+wavefunction#Hasebe08"} Hasebe 2008
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Laughlin+wavefunction#GromovMartinecRyu20"} Gromov, Martinec &amp; Ryu 2020 (13)
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The argument of the super-Laughlin wavefunction
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperLaughlinWavefunction"} (5)
              is indeed the difference of “super-positions” as seen in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-translation+group"} super-translation group
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "super-translation+group#eq:GroupLawIn1D"} there
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
